WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.900
- [Narrator] This big pink
building has an unusual name.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.280
Welcome to the Green Citadel.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.780
(bouncy, energetic music)

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.310
Located in the central
German City of Magdeburg

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.930
is an unusually bright complex
of 55 residential apartments,

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.391
shops, cafes, a hotel, and a preschool.

00:00:21.391 --> 00:00:24.040
The Green Citadel took
two years to complete

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.770
and was one of the first
prefabricated slab buildings

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:28.440
constructed in Germany.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.430
The bright pink contrasts with the roof,

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.923
which during the warmer seasons
is an entirely green garden.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:39.920
No two pillars or doors are
the same within the complex.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.983
Each is uniquely shaped or mosaicked.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.890
Created by the late Austrian architect,

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.020
Friedensreich Hundertwasser,
it was his last work

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.460
before he passed.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.340
In his own words, he describes the place

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.407
as an "oasis for humanity and nature

00:00:53.407 --> 00:00:55.757
"in a sea of rational houses."

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:05.192
(bell chiming)

